method: 'GET',
body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Alice' })
});
According to HTTP specifications, GET requests are intended to retrieve data only. Most
browsers and servers will ignore the body of a GET request. Data for GET requests should be
sent via Query Parameters (e.g., ?name=Alice).

Specificity is calculated as (ID count, Class count, Element count). Option C has one ID, one
class, and one element (1, 1, 1). Option B has one ID (1, 0, 0). (1,1,1) is higher than (1,0,0).
